window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-56e8c36f028eb49f"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"create-a-site\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">创建网站</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>先用文字描述你想在 ChatGPT 或 Codex 中构建什么。然后查看生成的第一个版本，并逐步调整完善。</p> <p><a id=\"get-started-with-sites\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"sites\">开始使用 Sites</h2> <p>在网页端或桌面应用中打开 ChatGPT。在提示词中写上“website”（网站），或提及 <code>@Sites</code>，即可启动 Sites 工作流。例如，你可以要求它为运营团队创建一个项目申请看板：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">为我的运营团队构建一个项目申请仪表板网站。让团队成员能够提交申请、查看每项申请的负责人、更新状态并筛选列表。要求用户使用其工作区账户登录，并确保申请数据在多次访问之间都能保存。\n</code></pre> <p><strong>ChatGPT Enterprise 用户注意：</strong> 工作区管理员必须先为你的工作区或角色启用 Sites，你才能创建网站。如果你看不到 Sites，请向管理员确认访问权限。<a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">查看 Sites 管理指南</a>。</p> <p>项目申请看板只是一个示例。你可以按下面的流程，改为构建自己需要的网站。</p> <ol> <li>描述网站</li> </ol> <p>告诉 ChatGPT 这个网站面向哪些人，以及你希望访客能做什么。提供网站需要使用的文档或数据。以项目申请看板为例，你可以提供申请示例、负责人和状态标签。</p> <ol> <li>检查网站</li> </ol> <p>试用你要求的各项操作，并对照源材料检查内容和结果。对于申请看板，你可以提交一项申请、更改其状态，或按负责人筛选。确认网站如何使用和保存信息。</p> <ol> <li>调整网站</li> </ol> <p>告诉 ChatGPT 你想修改什么；如果有帮助，也可以提供截图或参考网站。例如，你可以说：“把负责人和状态筛选器放到申请列表上方。”</p> <ol> <li>管理并分享网站</li> </ol> <p>返回 <strong>Sites</strong>，重新打开或编辑网站。发布前，请完成<a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59?anchor=_2\">发布前检查与分享检查（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。选择允许哪些人访问，并以目标访客的身份检查已发布的链接。</p> <p><a id=\"sites\"></a> <strong>查找 Sites 并在预览中编辑</strong></p> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中打开 <strong>Sites</strong>。你可以通过提示词或兼容的本地项目开始创建网站，然后回到 Sites 页面进行管理。</p> <p>在网页端，选择 <strong>More（更多）</strong> &gt; <strong>Sites</strong>，或直接前往 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的 Sites（需联网）</a>，查找你创建的网站。 在预览中选择 <strong>Edit（编辑）</strong>。在 <strong>Describe website edits（描述网站修改）</strong>下方，说明你想做哪些更改。如果需要补充背景信息，可以使用 <strong>Screenshot（截图）</strong>或 <strong>Add files and more（添加文件等）</strong>。</p> <p>Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展没有独立的 Sites 管理界面。请在 ChatGPT 网页端或桌面应用中创建、保存、部署和管理网站。你仍然可以使用 CLI 或 IDE 扩展，在发布前编辑和测试本地项目。</p> <p>Sites 的每个部署 URL 都指向生产环境。如果你想先检查构建结果、暂不让它上线，可以要求 ChatGPT 保存一个不部署的版本。</p> <p><a id=\"save-records-and-progress\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">保存记录和进度</h2> <p>保存网站版本会保留其内容、设计和行为。访客申请、状态更新、上传文件和个人进度需要单独存储。告诉 ChatGPT 或 Codex 要保存什么，以及谁可以读取或修改这些内容。</p> <p>对于共享记录或个人记录，请要求使用由服务器强制执行的访问规则。检查更新在重新加载页面后是否仍然保存，并使用不同账户确认每个人的访问权限。隐藏按钮并不能保护其背后的记录数据。</p> <p>对于你提供的文件，请说明网站应使用文件副本，还是应从源位置刷新文件。检查其中信息的最后更新时间。</p> <p>有关存储和登录选项，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2?anchor=choose-storage-and-sign-in-features\">数据与连接</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"describe-your-site\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"build-on-and-edit-your-site\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"tips-for-building-your-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">构建网站的建议</h2> <ul> <li><strong>使用源材料。</strong> 附上网站应使用的文件、链接、定义和公式。要求 ChatGPT 或 Codex 标出缺失的信息，不要自行补全。</li> <li><strong>描述空白状态和错误状态。</strong> 说明访客在搜索无结果、表单未填写完整或连接的应用不可用时应该看到什么，并提供重试或修正问题的方法。</li> <li><strong>提供视觉参考。</strong> 附上截图或页面链接，并指出你想采用的细节，例如紧凑卡片或搜索框的位置。还可以提供品牌颜色、字体或写作规范。</li> <li><strong>考虑手机屏幕。</strong> 说明卡片、表格和表单在窄屏上应如何排列。检查导航、筛选器和表单控件能否正常使用，避免必须横向滚动。</li> <li><strong>标明示例数据。</strong> 如果最终内容尚未准备好，请要求把示例记录明确标为示例。分享网站前记得替换它们。</li> <li><strong>每次只改一项。</strong> 一次提出一项修改，并说明哪些内容必须保留。例如，移动筛选器时不要改变已保存记录、访问规则或现有操作。每次修改后都要测试受影响的交互。</li> </ul> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 示例展示（官方来源暂不可用）</a>提供了一些可以用 Sites 构建的 Web 应用示例。</p> <p><a id=\"example-prompts\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">提示词示例</h3> <p>对于资源中心，可以先写一个简短的提示词：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">为项目负责人构建一个资源中心网站，让他们可以按任务搜索项目启动资料。使用我附上的资源列表。保存一个不部署的版本，供我审阅。\n</code></pre> <p>你还可以补充访客操作、搜索规则和设计偏好，让要求更具体：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">为正在准备项目启动工作的负责人构建一个资源中心网站。使用我附上的资源列表，包括标题、描述、任务标签和来源链接。\n\n访客操作：\n\n- 选择一项任务，例如准备议程。\n- 在该任务对应的资源中搜索。\n- 选择一条结果以打开其来源链接。\n\n搜索规则：\n\n- 搜索框为空时，显示所选任务的全部资源。\n- 未选择任务时，显示完整列表。\n- 没有匹配项时，提供清除筛选条件的方式，并显示我提供的列表中的帮助联系人。\n- 将缺少标题或链接的条目标记出来，供我审阅。\n- 访客返回时，可以重置搜索筛选条件。\n\n设计偏好：\n\n- 使用白色背景和深色文字。描述保持为一句话，布局应适合手机浏览。\n- 如果我提供参考屏幕截图，请据此安排搜索框位置和紧凑的资源卡片。\n- 如果我提供品牌指南，请使用其中的强调色。\n\n保存一个不部署的版本，以便我审阅布局并试用搜索功能。\n</code></pre> <p>对于现有项目，可以要求 ChatGPT 检查兼容性并做好发布准备：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 Sites 部署此项目。检查项目是否兼容，完成必要的修改，并提供部署 URL。\n</code></pre> <p>如果网站需要记住记录或上传文件，请在请求中明确说明：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">为这个游戏添加玩家分数和头像上传功能，并确保分数与已上传头像在用户下次访问时仍然保留。\n</code></pre>","en":"<h1 id=\"create-a-site\">Create a site</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Start by describing what you want to build in ChatGPT or Codex. Then review the first version and refine it as you go.</p> <h2 id=\"get-started-with-sites\">Get started with sites</h2> <p>Open ChatGPT on the web or in the desktop app. Include the word \"website\" in your prompt or mention <code>@Sites</code> to start the sites workflow. For example, you could ask for a project request dashboard for an operations team:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Build a project request dashboard website for my operations team. Let team members submit requests, see who owns each one, update the status, and filter the list. Require people to sign in with their workspace account, and keep the request data saved between visits.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>For ChatGPT Enterprise users:</strong> A workspace admin must enable sites for your workspace or role before you can create one. If you don't see sites, ask your admin about access. <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">See the Sites administration guide</a>.</p> <p>The dashboard is one example. You can adapt the following flow to the site you want to build.</p> <ol> <li>Describe the site</li> </ol> <p>Tell ChatGPT who the site is for and what you'd like people to do. Share the documents or data it needs. For a request dashboard, you might include sample requests, owners, and status labels.</p> <ol> <li>Review the site</li> </ol> <p>Try the actions you asked for, and check the content and results against your source material. For the dashboard, you might submit a request, change its status, or filter by owner. Confirm how the site uses and saves information.</p> <ol> <li>Refine the site</li> </ol> <p>Tell ChatGPT what you'd like to change, and share a screenshot or reference site if it would help. For the dashboard, you might ask: “Put the owner and status filters above the request list.”</p> <ol> <li>Manage and share the site</li> </ol> <p>Return to <strong>sites</strong> to reopen or edit the site. Before publishing, follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59?anchor=review-before-you-share\">review and sharing checks (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>. Choose who can visit and check the published link as an intended visitor.</p> <p><a id=\"find-sites-and-edit-in-the-preview\"></a> <strong>Find sites and edit in the preview</strong></p> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, open <strong>sites</strong>. You can start a site from a prompt or from a compatible local project, then return to the sites view to manage it.</p> <p>On the web, select <strong>More</strong> &gt; <strong>sites</strong>, or go directly to <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sites in ChatGPT (online)</a>, to find sites you've created. In the preview, select <strong>Edit</strong>. Under <strong>Describe website edits</strong>, describe the changes you want. Use <strong>Screenshot</strong> or <strong>Add files and more</strong> when more context would help.</p> <p>Sites doesn't have a standalone management view in the Codex CLI or IDE extension. Use ChatGPT on the web or in the desktop app to create, save, deploy, and manage a site. You can still use the CLI or IDE extension to edit and test a local project before publishing it.</p> <p>Every sites deployment URL is a production deployment. If you want to review a build before it becomes live, ask ChatGPT to save a version without deploying it.</p> <h2 id=\"save-records-and-progress\">Save records and progress</h2> <p>Saving a site version preserves its content, design, and behavior. Visitor requests, status updates, uploaded files, and personal progress need their own storage. Tell ChatGPT or Codex what to save and who should be able to read or change it.</p> <p>For shared or personal records, ask for access rules enforced on the server. Check that updates stay saved after reload, and use separate accounts to confirm each person's access. Hiding a button doesn't protect the underlying record.</p> <p>For supplied files, specify whether the site should use a copy or refresh from the source. Check when the information was last updated.</p> <p>For storage and sign-in options, see <a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2?anchor=choose-storage-and-sign-in-features\">Data and connections</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"describe-your-site\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"build-on-and-edit-your-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"tips-for-building-your-site\">Tips for building your site</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Use your source material.</strong> Attach the files, links, definitions, and formulas the site should use. Ask ChatGPT or Codex to flag missing information instead of filling it in.</li> <li><strong>Describe empty and error states.</strong> Explain what visitors should see when a search has no matches, a form is incomplete, or a connected app is unavailable. Include a way to retry or correct the problem.</li> <li><strong>Share a visual reference.</strong> Attach a screenshot or link to a page, and point out the details you want to use, such as compact cards or search placement. Include any brand colors, fonts, or writing guidelines.</li> <li><strong>Plan for phones.</strong> Describe how cards, tables, and forms should fit a narrow screen. Check that navigation, filters, and form controls remain usable without horizontal scrolling.</li> <li><strong>Label sample data.</strong> If the final content isn't ready, ask for sample records labeled as examples. Replace them before sharing the site.</li> <li><strong>Make focused changes.</strong> Ask for one change at a time and say what to keep. For example, move a filter without changing the saved records, access rules, or existing actions. Try the affected interaction after each change.</li> </ul> <p>The <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/showcase.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites showcase (official source unavailable)</a> shares example web apps you could build with Sites.</p> <h3 id=\"example-prompts\">Example prompts</h3> <p>For a resource hub, start with a short prompt:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Build a resource hub website where project leads can search our kickoff resources by task. Use the resource list I attach. Save a version without deploying it so I can review it.\n</code></pre> <p>You could expand that request with visitor actions, search rules, and design preferences:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Build a resource hub website for project leads preparing a kickoff. Use the resource list I attach, with its titles, descriptions, task labels, and source links.\n\nVisitor actions:\n\n- Choose a task, such as preparing an agenda.\n- Search within that task's resources.\n- Select a result to open its source link.\n\nSearch rules:\n\n- When the search is empty, show all resources for the selected task.\n- If no task is selected, show the full list.\n- If there are no matches, offer a way to clear the filters and show the help contact from my list.\n- Flag entries with missing titles or links for my review.\n- Search filters can reset when the visitor returns.\n\nDesign preferences:\n\n- Use a white background and dark text. Keep descriptions to one sentence, with a layout that works on a phone.\n- If I provide a reference screenshot, use it for the search placement and compact resource cards.\n- If I provide a brand guide, use its accent color.\n\nSave a version without deploying it so I can review the layout and try the search.\n</code></pre> <p>For an existing project, ask ChatGPT to check compatibility and prepare it for publishing:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Deploy this project with sites. Check whether it is compatible, make any required changes, and give me the deployment URL.\n</code></pre> <p>When a site needs to remember records or uploaded files, include that in your request:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add player scores and avatar uploads to this game. Keep the scores and uploaded avatars between visits.\n</code></pre>"};
